A||||12||RossT||trunk light cover||||1||
Z||000000||RossT||03-03-2000||05:05 PM||||Simple question, how do you remove the clear<BR>cover to get at the bulb.  Does it slide up,down,left or right. It looks to be on very tight and I do not want to break any plastic tabs.  Also where in the trunk is the switch that turns the light off when the deck lid is closed? (88gt)  Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||03-03-2000||05:09 PM||||I don't know how to take off the cover, but I believe the shut-off switch is the little black plastic tab in the lid latch.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||03-03-2000||06:18 PM||||Take a small, flat-bladed screwdriver and push it in one side.  That should release the side.  The light turns off when you close the trunk lid.  If it doesn't, something is wrong with the wiring.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gokart||03-03-2000||09:38 PM||||Removed the cover to change the light bulb when I first got my GT and the whole light assembly fell down into the hole in the firewall. Can't get it! So I'm in the dark till I find a replacement or put in a tacky looking aftermarket light.||||reg||8
Z||000004||RossT||03-03-2000||09:50 PM||||Thanks for the info guys.  Monkey, I know the<BR>light is suppose to go off when the lid is closed but where in the heck is the switch that turns the light off. Most cars have a dome light switch in the door jam, but where the heck is this switch in a fiero trunk?||||reg||1
Z||000005||RossT||03-03-2000||09:52 PM||||Gokart, couldn't you use some kind of coathanger of thin bendable wire that you could snag it??||||reg||1
Z||000006||Gokart||03-04-2000||06:04 AM||||Thanks Ross, I'll try that but I think it fell to far down. All the way down!||||reg||3
Z||000007||Carrolles||03-04-2000||07:11 AM||||On my 85SE the trunk light/lid ajar switch is just to  the rear of the left strut tower.  It looks like a door jam light switch and has two wires connected, one for the light and one for the lid ajar signal.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Bill Osmer||03-05-2000||12:35 PM||||The engine compartment light is activated on my 86GT by a small _switch_ in the latch of the engine cover. It can be verified by using your finger to move it to OFF (or back to ON when released) - it's a small black spring-loaded lever on the driver's side of the latch. It's also provides the signal to the "ajar" lamp on the IP.||||reg||4
Z||000009||pherder||03-05-2000||03:20 PM||||My advise (on 86-88s)is to look UP!!!  No, higher!  The switch is in the latch assembly!<P>When showing off the car, I see lots of Fieros with the trunk light on.  One case it was on ALL DAY and by the time the show was over, yep ... car wouldn't start.<P>I pushed closed the little lever on the switch, drilled a very small hole thru it and the body of the switch and put a small nail into the hole.  That kept the light off during shows.  I found that since the trunk light was basically useless, I kept the nail in the switch all the time.<P>The earlier model Fieros (84-85) have it easlier, just remove one of the wires on the door jam style of switch to kill the light.  Or mount a switch to turn the switch off (then you could have another switch ... sorry, got carried away there ...)<P>Paul||||reg||10
Z||000010||RossT||03-06-2000||02:32 AM||||Thanks Pherder, I always have my trunk lid open, and I could not stand to have the light on all the time. I will check out the latch, I really don't want to crack the lense<BR>trying to remove the bulb.<BR>Ross||||reg||1
Z||000011||Raydar||03-07-2000||12:15 AM||||GoKart, There's a steel channel that goes across the front of the trunk. Not really noticeable until you pull out the carpet. The light is mounted in the center of it. When it fell in, it probably slid over to the left. That's where the wires (at least mine) come from. There's not much room for it to fall down. ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Gokart||03-07-2000||06:39 AM||||Thanks Raydar, I'll look for when I take the carpet out which I was planning on to clean soon anyway.||||reg||14
